    "introduction": "Ignacio Masllorens is a filmmaker and visual artist. He studied image and sound design at the University of Buenos Aires (UBA), where he currently teaches. His films and videos propose a reflective exploration of the internal mechanisms of cinematic storytelling, as well as the perception of time and space, drawing on materials such as found-footage and documentary records. His works have been screened at various film festivals and several venues including the Anthology Film Archives, the Cinémathèque française, the Filmmuseum München, ARCOmadrid Art Fair, and the Museo de Arte Latinoamericano de Buenos Aires (MALBA) among many others. He has received awards in visual arts competitions held by the Fortabat Foundation, the ArtHaus Foundation, the National Arts Fund, and the National Salon. In 2021, he won the Audience Award at the Biarritz Amérique Latine Festival for the film Fanny camina, co-directed with Alfredo Arias.",
